WEBVTT

00:24.465 --> 00:27.335
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

00:27.335 --> 00:32.065
I may just see the limits of the light.

00:32.065 --> 00:33.975
The mind of stardust

00:33.975 --> 00:39.805
What a small universe I live in

00:39.805 --> 00:47.355
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

00:47.355 --> 00:49.925
Multiplied and in confusion

00:49.925 --> 00:53.955
A colony dead inside its cage

00:53.955 --> 00:58.425
Shoot your cowardly dreams

00:58.425 --> 01:01.595
Loneliness... self-destruct!

01:01.595 --> 01:05.965
No matter what sacrifices we make

01:05.965 --> 01:09.805
for a future just beyond reach

01:09.805 --> 01:13.515
Let our hearts speak to each other

01:13.515 --> 01:16.815
deep down inside

01:16.815 --> 01:20.955
Though the days just one step behind

01:20.955 --> 01:23.955
will pass even farther from us

01:23.955 --> 01:31.015
You will be in my thoughts

01:42.205 --> 01:44.075
I'd managed to hide my identity as a human...

01:44.075 --> 01:47.645
and blend into beastman society,
when all of a sudden...

01:47.645 --> 01:51.885
the World Destruction
Committee showed up in my life.

01:51.885 --> 01:54.315
Everyone freeze! Stay right where you are!

01:55.855 --> 01:57.825
So annoying...

01:57.825 --> 02:00.355
I really wish you guys'd just quit it.

02:00.355 --> 02:04.095
Especially when this lunch
cost me everything I had!

02:04.095 --> 02:06.065
They called it a committee,
but as it turns out...

02:06.065 --> 02:10.605
there was only one member,
a girl named Morte Urshela.

02:10.605 --> 02:14.095
Take one more step and the beastman gets it!

02:18.905 --> 02:20.205
Fire!

02:25.345 --> 02:29.185
Morte was carrying something that she
said had the power to destroy the world.

02:29.185 --> 02:31.225
It was called the Destruct Code...

02:31.225 --> 02:34.095
and she was planning to use it!

02:34.095 --> 02:38.765
Will the world really be
annihilated if you use this?

02:38.765 --> 02:41.785
Yeah, if you know how to use it right.

02:43.565 --> 02:46.265
Morte was being chased
by a beastman organization...

02:46.265 --> 02:48.565
called the World Salvation Committee.

02:49.305 --> 02:51.745
Somehow I got caught up in
the fight between the two sides...

02:51.745 --> 02:57.805
and wound up having to flee the
World Salvation Committee along with Morte.

02:58.045 --> 03:02.075
I was just a guy with a
part-time job... so why me?

03:03.085 --> 03:05.225
We were joined by a battle-hardened
warrior from the Hero Guild...

03:05.225 --> 03:07.155
a bear named Toppy.

03:07.155 --> 03:11.625
And the three of us made our way to a
place on the edge of nowhere called Bonak.

03:11.625 --> 03:14.735
I have an idea! Why don't we
quit all that world destruction stuff

03:14.735 --> 03:17.305
and just go around helping
people like this instead?

03:17.305 --> 03:21.335
I mean, we always seem to wind up
helping someone in the end, anyway.

03:21.335 --> 03:27.475
The way this world is, we'd be helping
everyone by destroying it for them.

03:27.475 --> 03:28.815
From that moment...

03:28.815 --> 03:29.975
whether I wanted it or not...

03:29.975 --> 03:34.315
my journey with the World
Destruction Committee was about to begin!

03:34.315 --> 03:36.475
Or so we thought...

03:42.995 --> 03:45.665
There are two kinds of beastmen.

03:45.665 --> 03:48.525
Beastmen who rule over humans, and...

03:57.975 --> 03:59.805
Now don't you go givin' us no problems!

03:59.805 --> 04:02.375
Human scum...

04:02.375 --> 04:06.445
Course it's a shame about you,
bein' a beastman and all.

04:06.445 --> 04:09.985
What do you plan to do with us, bear-o?!

04:09.985 --> 04:13.125
Seems these guys callin' themselves
the World Salvation Committee

04:13.125 --> 04:14.625
really want your heads on a platter.

04:14.625 --> 04:17.965
And they're offerin' a heap of money.

04:17.965 --> 04:20.635
I don't care if you're the World
Destruction Committee or the PTA.

04:20.635 --> 04:23.695
To us you're manna from heaven.

04:24.905 --> 04:27.465
But you can't! Just wai...!

04:30.675 --> 04:32.045
I'll just tell you right now.

04:32.045 --> 04:35.575
Don't even think about tryin' to defy us.

04:35.575 --> 04:39.845
'Cuz they didn't say nuthin' 'bout
handin' you over in one piece.

04:41.255 --> 04:44.045
The exchange'll happen in two days.

04:51.065 --> 04:53.065
What do we do?

04:53.065 --> 04:54.565
Do I have to spell it out for you?!

04:54.565 --> 04:58.765
We make our escape before the
World Salvation Committee gets here!

05:05.945 --> 05:08.915
It wasn't me, you guys!

05:09.915 --> 05:11.645
It was me, bear-o.

05:11.685 --> 05:16.645
"There are Two Kinds of Beastmen"

05:16.855 --> 05:19.255
A prison run by wolves?

05:19.255 --> 05:22.595
It's a prison on the edge of nowhere.
In a place called Bonak.

05:22.595 --> 05:25.225
We received word from them yesterday

05:25.225 --> 05:28.865
that they'd captured three members
of the World Destruction Committee.

05:28.865 --> 05:32.865
Those three must have some
kind of luck, wouldn't you say?

05:32.865 --> 05:36.705
To wash up there, of all places.

05:36.705 --> 05:40.275
So? What did the prison people say?

05:40.275 --> 05:43.145
They wanted money.

05:43.145 --> 05:45.115
Oh, what a crude bunch they are!

05:45.115 --> 05:48.045
But we don't have to cater to the likes of them.

05:49.955 --> 05:52.655
We can just seize the prisoners by force!

05:52.655 --> 05:55.425
That's a bad habit of yours, Lia.

05:55.425 --> 05:58.825
Force is something you need to
choose the right time to employ.

05:58.825 --> 06:03.095
If money solves the problem,
isn't that more expedient for everyone?

06:08.105 --> 06:09.975
Gimme a break!

06:09.975 --> 06:13.245
How come I gotta be the
only one stuck in this hellhole?!

06:13.245 --> 06:15.145
What kind of place is this, anyway?

06:15.145 --> 06:17.685
From what I see, it's filled
with the worst of the worst!

06:17.685 --> 06:19.985
Over there... she's one of the ones
from the World Destruction Committee.

06:19.985 --> 06:22.785
Idiot! Don't look her in the eye!
You don't know what she might do to you!

06:22.785 --> 06:24.485
She looks scary...

06:33.265 --> 06:36.335
We're surrounded by high walls on all sides.

06:36.335 --> 06:41.435
Even if we could climb over, we'd
still have the armed guards to contend with.

06:41.435 --> 06:46.635
But on the other hand, it'd be pretty hard
to escape through that maze of a mine.

06:51.185 --> 06:53.045
What the hell you doin'?!

06:54.355 --> 06:56.485
It ain't bad enough you're a weakling...

06:56.485 --> 06:59.945
now you gotta go and...
make more work for me?!

07:03.895 --> 07:06.025
I-I'm s-sorry...

07:13.135 --> 07:15.405
Hey there, humans!

07:15.405 --> 07:17.875
Stop standin' 'round and wash up them dishes!

07:19.905 --> 07:22.415
Done... whew.

07:22.415 --> 07:24.245
Whoa, you better take those off the fire!

07:24.245 --> 07:25.985
Huh? Uh... Uh-huh...

07:25.985 --> 07:28.215
Look, those pots are boiling!

07:28.215 --> 07:30.985
Huh? Ah, uh-huh...

07:30.985 --> 07:33.025
Say, don't I know you from somewhere?

07:33.025 --> 07:38.225
- These plates go here, right?
- Isn't that guy one of the
World Destruction Committee ones?

07:38.225 --> 07:40.535
What's a beastman doing in a place like this?

07:40.535 --> 07:43.365
I'm tellin' ya, he's the
worst criminal in the world!

07:43.365 --> 07:47.865
From that World Destruction
Committee thing people been talkin' about...

07:49.105 --> 07:50.175
Hey, buddy!

07:50.175 --> 07:51.775
I understand how you feel...

07:51.775 --> 07:55.075
but you're a prisoner now,
so we can't have you slackin' off on the...

08:06.355 --> 08:08.625
Time to eat up!

08:12.425 --> 08:13.795
So?

08:13.795 --> 08:15.065
Mwo?

08:15.065 --> 08:16.465
Mwarencha mgwonna eat?

08:16.465 --> 08:20.105
I'm asking you... were
you able to find anything out?

08:20.105 --> 08:23.305
Some kind of secret passage?
Maybe something about the guards?

08:23.305 --> 08:25.545
Mwe guards mwalso thwought
mwis food was pwetty good.

08:25.545 --> 08:27.045
That's not what I mean!

08:27.045 --> 08:28.275
Fine, whatever!

08:28.275 --> 08:31.045
Toppy, what about you?

08:31.045 --> 08:33.315
The worst of the worst criminals in the world

08:33.315 --> 08:35.655
treated me like the super
worst of the worst, bear-o.

08:35.655 --> 08:38.485
And? What about the guards?

08:38.485 --> 08:42.125
As far as the guards go, they're afraid
of me and won't even get close, bear-o.

08:42.125 --> 08:44.715
That's not what I mean!

08:45.325 --> 08:47.435
Well it's a big deal to me, bear-o!

08:47.435 --> 08:53.565
- Toppy! Toppy! Toppy! Toppy!
- What kind of hero wins notoriety
in prison? You know of one, bear-o?!

08:54.635 --> 08:59.575
Okay, but right now we have to
focus on finding a way out of here.

09:03.345 --> 09:06.815
I saw a goods delivery
gate on one side of the mine.

09:06.815 --> 09:08.085
Of course there were guards...

09:08.085 --> 09:11.655
but if we get our weapons back,
I think we can bust our way through.

09:11.655 --> 09:14.295
All that's left is finding
a way out of this cell...

09:14.295 --> 09:16.455
and retrieving the Destruct Code.

09:16.455 --> 09:19.165
As far as the Destruct Code goes,
I know what room it's in, bear-o.

09:19.165 --> 09:22.635
All of our things were
piled in there together, bear-o.

09:22.635 --> 09:24.765
Okay, then. Next is...

09:24.765 --> 09:27.435
I think I might know where
they keep the key to our cell.

09:27.435 --> 09:29.975
Just now when I was bringing
the food to the guards' room...

09:29.975 --> 09:31.945
I saw a whole bunch of keys in there.

09:31.945 --> 09:33.605
Guards' room?

09:33.605 --> 09:36.315
It's just one floor down from here.

09:36.315 --> 09:39.185
But in terms of position,
it's the farthest room away from us.

09:39.185 --> 09:41.155
Way on the other side of the building.

09:49.895 --> 09:53.165
I guess that won't work without tools.

09:53.165 --> 09:55.495
I wonder if there's some way...

09:55.495 --> 10:00.805
Now that I think about it, some wild
bears dig holes in the ground for their dens.

10:03.075 --> 10:06.145
That's got nothing to do with me, bear-o.

10:06.145 --> 10:08.245
But don't you say "bear-o" all the time?

10:08.245 --> 10:11.405
And given your size...

10:16.055 --> 10:17.015
See?

10:17.015 --> 10:18.255
Count me out, bear-o.

10:18.255 --> 10:20.825
I can't go around acting like some bear, bear-o!

10:20.825 --> 10:22.655
Bear-o, bear-o... just shut up already!

10:22.655 --> 10:23.925
We don't have time to play games!

10:23.925 --> 10:27.985
Or would you rather live out your days in
this place with that notoriety you hate?!

10:33.035 --> 10:37.875
The world'd be better off if that girl just
stayed locked up in here forever, bear-o!

11:04.905 --> 11:08.105
One of the guards is
giving medicine to a prisoner.

11:08.105 --> 11:11.575
This is the first time I've ever seen
a beastman show kindness to a human!

11:11.575 --> 11:14.095
Morte? Are you asleep?

11:21.615 --> 11:26.285
I'm sorry I couldn't do
anything to help this afternoon.

11:26.285 --> 11:30.625
Don't feel bad... that kind
of thing happens all the time.

11:30.625 --> 11:34.795
Please, just don't think
that all beastmen are like that.

11:34.795 --> 11:39.235
Even worse, you're locked up in
here for a crime you didn't commit!

11:39.235 --> 11:40.935
But one day you'll be free and...

11:40.935 --> 11:43.005
I'm sorry, as a beastman

11:43.005 --> 11:45.405
I know I'm not in any kind of
position to be saying this to you, but...

11:46.905 --> 11:48.115
Sorry!

11:48.115 --> 11:50.275
But you're just so sincere!

11:50.275 --> 11:53.075
And your face is beet red.

11:59.755 --> 12:01.655
Thank you.

12:15.375 --> 12:17.205
You again.

12:17.205 --> 12:20.505
Always makin' more work for me!

12:20.505 --> 12:21.875
It seems that...

12:21.875 --> 12:24.105
talkin' don't work on you!

12:27.355 --> 12:28.955
You little...!

12:28.955 --> 12:31.185
Filthy human, you think you can defy me?!

12:31.185 --> 12:32.455
Well, it seems that...

12:32.455 --> 12:35.515
Talking just doesn't work on you.

12:39.495 --> 12:41.895
"Filthy human"...

12:41.895 --> 12:43.865
"Filthy beastman"...

12:43.865 --> 12:45.835
The whole thing makes me sick!

13:12.025 --> 13:15.895
The World Salvation Committee's supposed
to be comin' tomorrow mornin', ain't that right?

13:15.895 --> 13:19.265
Yes, sir. It appears they'll
be arriving right on schedule.

13:19.265 --> 13:20.435
The incident this afternoon...

13:20.435 --> 13:23.935
that World Destruction Committee
girl standing up to a guard...

13:23.935 --> 13:27.775
it could give the other prisoners ideas,
and we don' need no more uprisings.

13:27.775 --> 13:32.515
Tomorrow's a big day... better do some room
inspections and tighten down on discipline!

13:32.515 --> 13:34.075
Yes, sir...

13:50.265 --> 13:53.905
Room inspections. Can you help me out?

13:53.905 --> 13:56.235
At this time of night?

14:05.945 --> 14:07.315
Room inspections!

14:07.315 --> 14:09.115
Front and center!

14:27.105 --> 14:28.775
I said front and center!

14:28.775 --> 14:31.745
You deaf? Hurry and get out there!

14:38.415 --> 14:39.615
Wait!

14:39.615 --> 14:41.675
Don't move! Stand still!

14:47.625 --> 14:49.025
Oh no!

14:57.665 --> 14:59.035
Room inspection.

14:59.035 --> 15:01.095
Hurry up and get out front!

15:06.105 --> 15:08.015
How'd it go?

15:08.015 --> 15:09.505
Mgwot 'em.

15:27.835 --> 15:32.165
This tunnel leads to the mine shaft.

15:33.405 --> 15:35.635
Hook up with those three from
the World Destruction Committee

15:35.635 --> 15:38.235
and use this tunnel to get out of here.

15:39.575 --> 15:42.875
At the very end, as you exit the mine...

15:42.875 --> 15:46.045
there's a goods delivery gate just on the side.

15:47.345 --> 15:49.055
Obviously there'll be some guards...

15:49.055 --> 15:51.585
but if you're with the other three,
you should be able to bust through.

15:51.585 --> 15:53.415
That's crazy!

15:54.995 --> 15:56.655
Don't worry.

15:56.655 --> 16:00.595
This afternoon that girl threw
one of the guards like it was nothing.

16:00.595 --> 16:03.935
And besides, those three
aren't like the other prisoners.

16:03.935 --> 16:06.865
They don't really seem like bad people.

16:06.865 --> 16:10.335
I've been waiting a long time
for humans like them to appear.

16:10.335 --> 16:13.075
That's not it! I'm worried about you!

16:13.075 --> 16:16.445
If they ever found out about this...

16:16.445 --> 16:19.385
who knows what might happen to you!

16:19.385 --> 16:21.215
I've done some terrible things.

16:21.215 --> 16:23.585
This is the least I can do to make up that.

16:23.585 --> 16:26.555
Tonight, after the final rounds are over...

16:26.555 --> 16:28.955
I'll lead the three of them here myself.

16:28.955 --> 16:30.925
Please be ready.

16:30.925 --> 16:32.265
But wait!

16:32.265 --> 16:33.855
Farewell.

16:43.435 --> 16:44.965
He's gone.

16:45.745 --> 16:48.975
First we secure the Destruct Code!

16:56.415 --> 17:01.215
Oh, that's right! I need to
give them their things back.

17:08.935 --> 17:10.955
Everybody ready?

17:15.405 --> 17:18.175
Keep quiet!

17:18.175 --> 17:21.145
Keep your mouth shut and I won't take your life.

17:21.145 --> 17:23.115
B-But!

17:23.115 --> 17:25.635
I said keep quiet!

17:27.145 --> 17:28.915
As a hero...

17:28.915 --> 17:33.415
I can't look the other way when
someone lays hands on a helpless individual.

17:36.095 --> 17:40.625
So then, you're from the summer continent?

17:40.625 --> 17:44.365
Yeah, but I ain't been
back in ten years or more.

17:56.375 --> 17:58.435
I keep telling you, shut up...!

17:59.545 --> 18:01.285
Prisoners escaping!

18:01.285 --> 18:02.975
They found out?!

18:05.955 --> 18:06.625
Don't mo...!

18:06.625 --> 18:07.855
Don't move!

18:17.165 --> 18:19.395
What's happening?

18:33.645 --> 18:34.715
Give it up!

18:34.715 --> 18:35.985
Stand back!

18:35.985 --> 18:38.885
I'm the World Destruction Committee!

18:38.885 --> 18:43.415
And I think you know that countless
beastmen have already died by my hand!

18:44.925 --> 18:46.495
Wouldn't it be funny at this point

18:46.495 --> 18:48.535
if he turned out to be wearing fake
ears like someone else I know?

18:48.535 --> 18:50.435
Who cares about him! Shoot!

18:54.405 --> 18:56.235
Those three are pay dirt!

18:56.235 --> 18:58.245
Do not let 'em escape!

18:58.245 --> 19:00.275
But... but!

19:00.275 --> 19:02.075
That's an order!

19:02.075 --> 19:03.735
Shoot!

19:11.955 --> 19:13.755
Look what you've gone and done!

19:13.755 --> 19:16.225
Now the plan's no good!

19:16.925 --> 19:19.725
There was no need to go
busting out through the front door!

19:19.725 --> 19:21.785
Damn, where is she?

19:23.595 --> 19:25.435
What happened?

19:33.145 --> 19:35.045
Run!

19:36.775 --> 19:38.485
Get that one too!

19:38.485 --> 19:40.285
Toppy!

19:40.285 --> 19:43.745
Time to show your stuff!

20:07.575 --> 20:09.235
We're coming through!

20:31.435 --> 20:35.205
What kind of miser can't
even protect his own money?

20:35.205 --> 20:37.205
No treatment for this one, I'm guessing.

20:37.205 --> 20:40.475
And I was just starting to
think this mission was finally over.

20:40.475 --> 20:41.945
Huh?

20:41.945 --> 20:43.935
I think punishment is called for.

20:56.725 --> 20:59.825
It kinda seems like we got you
two mixed up in our problems.

20:59.825 --> 21:00.995
We're really sorry.

21:00.995 --> 21:04.165
Not at all. I'm glad it worked out like this.

21:04.165 --> 21:08.205
I'm afraid you're probably gonna
have a lot more to deal with from now on.

21:08.205 --> 21:09.675
Don't worry about us.

21:09.675 --> 21:12.305
I've learned something from the three of you.

21:12.305 --> 21:14.245
I've learned that even if
people are from different tribes...

21:14.245 --> 21:16.045
as long as they just work together...

21:16.045 --> 21:19.245
they can overcome any hardship.

21:23.085 --> 21:25.425
What's so funny?

21:25.425 --> 21:27.085
Nothing.

21:28.895 --> 21:30.755
All right then, take care!

21:30.755 --> 21:32.695
You take care too!

21:32.695 --> 21:34.525
Cheers, bear-o.

21:44.035 --> 21:46.075
So then...

21:46.075 --> 21:48.905
Morte, where do we go from...

21:58.925 --> 22:02.295
That was the... spring continent!

22:02.295 --> 22:04.695
All the places we've been
so far have been a real drag...

22:04.695 --> 22:06.765
and I'm ready for a change.

22:06.765 --> 22:08.525
Let's go!

22:21.105 --> 22:24.615
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.615 --> 22:27.745
The end of the green earth

22:27.745 --> 22:33.825
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.825 --> 22:36.955
now plunged into darkness

22:36.955 --> 22:40.165
The memories will pile up

22:40.165 --> 22:46.165
like mounds of rubble

22:46.165 --> 22:49.405
Mutual encounters

22:49.405 --> 22:52.475
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.475 --> 22:55.615
Interwoven words

22:55.615 --> 22:58.745
People hurting each other

22:58.745 --> 23:10.855
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.695 --> 23:17.535
Living this moment against the world

23:17.535 --> 23:20.535
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.535 --> 23:26.105
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.105 --> 23:29.675
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.675 --> 23:33.215
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.215 --> 23:39.185
Until we reach

23:39.185 --> 23:50.795
the promised land just beyond

23:52.205 --> 23:54.205
In a little town on the spring continent...

23:54.205 --> 23:56.575
there was a single blooming cherry tree.

23:56.575 --> 23:59.475
It's said that in order to
produce its lovely blossoms,

23:59.475 --> 24:01.875
the cherry tree fed on
the lifeblood of beastmen...

24:02.975 --> 24:05.415
and the angry spirits of the beastmen
who lost their lives to the tree...

24:05.415 --> 24:07.585
still wander the land of the living...

24:07.585 --> 24:12.055
and bring terrible misfortune
upon any who dare injure the tree.

24:12.055 --> 24:15.155
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 4:

24:15.155 --> 24:17.025
"There Are Two Kinds of Humans."

24:17.025 --> 24:20.685
I don't go in for all that
superstitious nonsense, bear-o!
